 "remarks": "Recently renovated 4-bedroom, 2 bath home spanning three floors in downtown Greenwich, CT just steps from Greenwich Avenue and Greenwich Train Station. This is the private back house of a two-family property, with its own driveway access and a fully private backyard - outdoor space. The main level offers an open-concept living and dining area, plus a side office/playroom that closes off via a sliding barn door for flexible work-from-home or multi-use flexibility. Both the main living area and the side room open onto a private balcony overlooking the backyard, and a small creek - a rare pocket of privacy in the heart of downtown Greenwich. A full bathroom with shower completes this level. The upper floor holds three well-sized bedrooms, a full bathroom, and a dedicated laundry room. On the ground level, a converted carport features 5 garage doors that fully open to create a versatile indoor-outdoor room - ideal as a home gym, playroom, or entertaining space for most of the year (unheated). The private backyard gives the property a secluded, tucked-away feel despite its downtown location.  Location is unbeatable: just steps to the Greenwich train station, Greenwich Library, restaurants, parks, multiple supermarkets, gyms, and Greenwich Avenue shopping and dining. Nearby daycare centers add everyday convenience. Greenwich residents also enjoy access to town beaches, ferry service to the islands, and park passes for Tod's Point",
